{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["Its ledge — the recess of the altar. For it narrows above, to walk along that recess around the altar. And also in halakhah the term is used this way in the laws of everyday slaughter, so much so that the little projections and engraved designs on vessels, and the indentations made in them, are called by this name." "To the half of the altar — to distinguish between the upper bloods and the lower ones. And your mnemonic: the bird burnt-offering above, the bird sin-offering below. And with animals, the reverse: sin-offering above and burnt-offering below. All of this is in tractate Zevahim."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:17.954944104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}